  "title": "Hide what you hate, track what you love: super dislikes and per-classifier notifications",
  "summary": "<p>NewsBlur’s Intelligence Trainer has always had a simple rule: thumbs up beats thumbs down. If a story matches both a liked and a disliked classifier, the story shows up in Focus. That works well most of the time. But sometimes you run into a topic, author, or tag that you absolutely never want to see, and a regular thumbs down isn’t enough because a single thumbs up from another classifier overrides it.</p> Today I’m shipping two features that give the Intelligence Trainer more teeth: supe...",
